-         The `FromDigits` given which makes `val x: 0.0 ~ 1.0 = 0.2` typecheck; it needs
-         `scala.language.experimental.genericNumberLiterals`. A literal below the lower bound
-         is error `↯/s.16.4`, _the value `v` is less than the lower bound for this value, `min`_, and
-         one above the upper bound error `↯/s.16.3`, _the value `v` is greater than the upper bound for
-         this value, `max`_; bounds which are not `Double` literal types are errors `↯/s.16.1` and `↯/s.16.2`.
-         Both bounds are inclusive.
+       detail
+           Le given `FromDigits` qui fait passer la vérification de types à
+           `val x: 0.0 ~ 1.0 = 0.2` ; il nécessite
+           `scala.language.experimental.genericNumberLiterals`. Un littéral inférieur à la borne
+           inférieure est l'erreur `↯/s.16.4`, _the value `v` is less than the lower bound for this
+           value, `min`_, et un littéral supérieur à la borne supérieure l'erreur `↯/s.16.3`, _the
+           value `v` is greater than the upper bound for this value, `max`_ ; des bornes qui ne
+           sont pas des types littéraux `Double` sont les erreurs `↯/s.16.1` et `↯/s.16.2`. Les
+           deux bornes sont inclusives.

